, +1.8% in Q1 2026, then −4%.\n- **Voltaris shipments:** They fell 9% in Q2, the steepest among large makers.\n- **Market share:** Share fell from 31% to 27% in Q2 2026, a loss of 4 points. Tarnwell and imports gained.\n- **Revenue:** Quarterly revenue ran C$905M, C$960M, C$980M and C$890M from 2025Q3 to 2026Q2. The last four quarters sum to about C$3.74B. The Q2 drop of about 9% from Q1 matches the shipment decline.\n\n**Implied 2027 revenue**\n- **Run rate:** Q2 revenue of C$890M annualizes to about C$3.56B.\n- **Hitting guidance:** C$4.2B means about C$1.05B per quarter. That is about 18% above the Q2 run rate and about 7% above the best recent quarter, in a shrinking market.\n- **Share arithmetic:** If share stays at 27%, revenue sits near the Q2 level, which is C$3.5–3.6B. Reaching C$4.2B would need a recovery to about 31% share, or industry growth of about 15–18%. Neither is supported by the shipment data.\n\n**Caveats**\n- **Orders lead shipments:** Shipments trail orders by about two quarters. A separate document, n2's H1 2026 orders filing (n2.d2), reports H1 orders up 11% year on year. That could support a shipment rebound in late 2026 and 2027. I have not read it myself; the other node covers it.\n- **Order recovery:** Even if orders lift 2027 shipments by 10% over the Q2 run rate, revenue reaches only about C$3.9B. The industry data alone does not get Voltaris to C$4.2B.\n- **Price and mix:** Price and mix could add revenue beyond what shipment volumes imply. I have no data on either.","ttft_ms":1824,"type":"result","duration_ms":19837,"uuid":"dbf7dcf9-742d-48c6-97f4-95da69044e04","ttft_stream_ms":946,"time_to_request_ms":58,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":3,"resume_other":1,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":7,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":2,"tool_pool_refresh":2,"init_message":5,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":0,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"reque